{"nodes": [{"id": "openspec_changes_harden_server_security_design_harden_server_security", "label": "Design: Harden Server Security", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "openspec/changes/harden-server-security/design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "openspec_changes_harden_server_security_design_d1_native_env_reading", "label": "D1: Native env reading without mandatory dotenv", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "openspec/changes/harden-server-security/design.md", "source_location": "## Decisions > D1", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "config/config.js reads process.env directly with a requireEnv(name) helper that throws at startup if the variable is missing. dotenv as a mandatory dependency was rejected because it would be a new dependency in a legacy Node >= 6 project; .env.example documents the variables. Only direct-security variables (KEY_REQUEST_AUTH) are required; the rest have non-sensitive defaults or disable the feature (e-mail without credentials becomes sendEmail: false with a warning)."}, {"id": "openspec_changes_harden_server_security_design_d2_cors_allowlist", "label": "D2: CORS allowlist in existing manual middleware", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "openspec/changes/harden-server-security/design.md", "source_location": "## Decisions > D2", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Keep the manual middleware in index.js (no cors package) but echo the request Origin only when present in CORS_ORIGINS (comma split, trimmed); no match means no CORS headers. The cors package was rejected to minimize new dependencies since the manual middleware is about 10 lines."}, {"id": "openspec_changes_harden_server_security_design_d3_interceptor_fix", "label": "D3: Fix interceptor without changing token contract", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "openspec/changes/harden-server-security/design.md", "source_location": "## Decisions > D3", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Wrap CryptoJS.AES.decrypt + JSON.parse in try/catch returning 401 on failure; make the checkLogin callback fire on the failure path too (today only success invokes it, hanging the request); standardize 401 for missing/invalid token or rejected credentials and 403 for onlyLocalhost violations (was 500), with generic body via ResponseData.errorResponse. The AES token format (email+password inside) stays unchanged for client compatibility \u2014 redesigning it is a known weakness deferred to a future change."}, {"id": "openspec_changes_harden_server_security_design_d4_body_limit", "label": "D4: Configurable payload limit with 1mb default", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "openspec/changes/harden-server-security/design.md", "source_location": "## Decisions > D4", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "BODY_LIMIT with default '1mb' applied to bodyParser.json and bodyParser.urlencoded, replacing the 50mb limit that eased DoS. Deploys that genuinely need large payloads set the variable explicitly."}, {"id": "openspec_changes_harden_server_security_design_d5_direct_removals", "label": "D5: Remove spawn monkey-patch and hardcoded gateway IP", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "openspec/changes/harden-server-security/design.md", "source_location": "## Decisions > D5", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The child_process.spawn monkey-patch (IIFE at the end of index.js) was debug instrumentation logging possibly sensitive arguments \u2014 removed entirely. The hardcoded internal IP 10.200.1.190 moves to GATEWAY_HOST/GATEWAY_PORT, with current values documented only in .env.example, not in code."}, {"id": "openspec_changes_harden_server_security_design_key_request_auth", "label": "KEY_REQUEST_AUTH Environment Variable", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "openspec/changes/harden-server-security/design.md", "source_location": "## Decisions > D1", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Encryption key for the request authentication token; the only mandatory environment variable \u2014 the server refuses to start without it, replacing the hardcoded keyRequestAutentication secret."}, {"id": "openspec_changes_harden_server_security_design_spawn_monkey_patch", "label": "child_process.spawn Monkey-Patch (removed)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "openspec/changes/harden-server-security/design.md", "source_location": "## Context", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Debug instrumentation in index.js that logged all spawn arguments to the console, a potential leak of sensitive data; removed by this change."}], "edges": [{"source": "openspec_changes_harden_server_security_design_harden_server_security", "target": "openspec_changes_harden_server_security_design_d1_native_env_reading", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "openspec/changes/harden-server-security/design.md", "source_location": "## Decisions", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "openspec_changes_harden_server_security_design_harden_server_security", "target": "openspec_changes_harden_server_security_design_d2_cors_allowlist", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "openspec/changes/harden-server-security/design.md", "source_location": "## Decisions", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "openspec_changes_harden_server_security_design_harden_server_security", "target": "openspec_changes_harden_server_security_design_d3_interceptor_fix", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "openspec/changes/harden-server-security/design.md", "source_location": "## Decisions", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "openspec_changes_harden_server_security_design_harden_server_security", "target": "openspec_changes_harden_server_security_design_d4_body_limit", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "openspec/changes/harden-server-security/design.md", "source_location": "## Decisions", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "openspec_changes_harden_server_security_design_harden_server_security", "target": "openspec_changes_harden_server_security_design_d5_direct_removals", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "openspec/changes/harden-server-security/design.md", "source_location": "## Decisions", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "openspec_changes_harden_server_security_design_harden_server_security", "target": "openspec_changes_harden_server_security_proposal_harden_server_security", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": "openspec/changes/harden-server-security/design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "openspec_changes_harden_server_security_design_d1_native_env_reading", "target": "openspec_changes_harden_server_security_design_key_request_auth", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "openspec/changes/harden-server-security/design.md", "source_location": "## Decisions > D1", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "openspec_changes_harden_server_security_design_d5_direct_removals", "target": "openspec_changes_harden_server_security_design_spawn_monkey_patch", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "openspec/changes/harden-server-security/design.md", "source_location": "## Decisions > D5", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "openspec_changes_harden_server_security_design_d1_native_env_reading", "target": "openspec_changes_harden_server_security_spec